            <ArticleTitle>The effect of preoperative epidural morphine on postoperative analgesia in children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>598-600</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="IMPLICATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">We examined the effects of preoperative epidural morphine associated with general anesthesia on postoperative morphine requirements. Twenty-one children older than 6 yr scheduled for major surgery were randomly assigned to two groups, a control group and an epidural group that received a single epidural morphine injection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
